    rdf:value """to expiate my crimes in the desert, and Bernhard (very sensibly!) advised me to work them off here, in my actual life, by unselfishness, energy and absolute uprightness. This is both harder and less dramatic, but I will try. 
Friday Nov. 5. 1897.
Worked in the morning, cataloguing notes etc. Bernhard called on Dr. Baldwin and Mr. Benn in the afternoon and I had a walk. The weather glorious. In the evening we read long letters from Miss Anstruther-Thomson and Miss Paget denying that they had ever taken anything from Bernhard’s conversation or writings. Miss Thomson’s letter seemed honest, but incredibly """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 153 ;
